      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HARD SNIFF STYLE (1) has some solid form under his belt and proved too classy last time to win by 0.8 lengths at Bulli in a handy 19.40 beating Calla Muffin. Consistent performer from this draw with a win and five minor placings to his credit. Shapes as a top winning chance on latest effort. CLUSTER ONE (2) was strongly fancied latest and proved too good with a 0.8 lengths win at Gunnedah in a handy 19.93. Draws to advantage and in form and has the ability. Can make it two on the bounce. ZIPPING DOWNEY (7) turned spotting a big start finishing seventh (30.44) last time in a Grade 5 at Nowra. Goes well out of this box with a win and three minor placings. Leading chance. TAP OUT RUSTY (3) can sneak into the finish.",
